{"name":"Snuff","hex":"#e4d7e5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"snuff","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Finely ground or pulverized tobacco (or other plant derivative) intended for use by being sniffed or snorted into the nose.","Fine-ground or minced tobacco, dry or moistened, intended for use by placing a pinch behind the lip or beneath the tongue."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To inhale through the nose.","To turn up the nose and inhale air, as an expression of contempt; hence, to take offense."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snuff"}],"entries":[{"title":"Snuff (tobacco)","blocks":[{"text":"Snuff is a type of smokeless tobacco product made from finely ground or pulverized tobacco leaves.\nIt is snorted or \"sniffed\" into the nasal cavity, delivering nicotine and a flavored scent to the user. Traditionally, it is sniffed or inhaled lightly after a pinch of snuff is either placed onto the back surface of the hand, held pinched between thumb and index finger, or held by a specially made \"snuffing\" device."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Snuff_assortment-2.jpg/330px-Snuff_assortment-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snuff_(tobacco)"},{"title":"Dipping tobacco","blocks":[{"text":"Dipping tobacco  is a type of finely ground or shredded, moistened smokeless tobacco product. It is commonly and idiomatically known as dip. Dipping tobacco is used by placing a pinch, or \"dip\", of tobacco between the lip and the gum. The act of using it is called dipping. Dipping tobacco is colloquially called snus, chaw, snuff, rub, or fresh leaf, among other terms; because of this, it is sometimes confused with other tobacco products, namely dry snuff."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Smokeless_tobacco_is_no_healthier_than_smoking_130226-M-ZB219-007.jpg/330px-Smokeless_tobacco_is_no_healthier_than_smoking_130226-M-ZB219-007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dipping_tobacco"},{"title":"Snuff (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Snuff is a 1976 splatter film directed by Michael Findlay and Horacio Fredriksson. Originally an exploitation film loosely based on the 1969 murders committed by the Manson Family, it is most notorious for being falsely marketed as if it were an actual snuff film. The controversy about the film was deliberately manufactured to attract publicity: it prompted an investigation by the New York County District Attorney, who determined that the murder shown in the film was fake. This picture contributed to the urban legend of snuff films, although the concept did not originate with it."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9c/Poster_of_the_movie_Snuff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snuff_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/A_17th_century_snuff_shop_in_Amsterdam.jpg/500px-A_17th_century_snuff_shop_in_Amsterdam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/A_17th_century_snuff_shop_in_Amsterdam.jpg/1280px-A_17th_century_snuff_shop_in_Amsterdam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/A_17th_century_snuff_shop_in_Amsterdam.jpg/500px-A_17th_century_snuff_shop_in_Amsterdam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 17th-century snuff shop in Amsterdam","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_17th_century_snuff_shop_in_Amsterdam.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Schnupftabak_lose.jpg/500px-Schnupftabak_lose.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Schnupftabak_lose.jpg/1280px-Schnupftabak_lose.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Schnupftabak_lose.jpg/500px-Schnupftabak_lose.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Several types and consistencies of snuff tobacco","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASchnupftabak_lose.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Snuff_Shooting_Device.jpg/500px-Snuff_Shooting_Device.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Snuff_Shooting_Device.jpg/1280px-Snuff_Shooting_Device.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Snuff_Shooting_Device.jpg/500px-Snuff_Shooting_Device.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Spring-loaded novelty device used to shoot snuff directly into one's nostrils","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASnuff_Shooting_Device.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Angelica_Kauffmann_002.png/500px-Angelica_Kauffmann_002.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Angelica_Kauffmann_002.png/1280px-Angelica_Kauffmann_002.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Angelica_Kauffmann_002.png/500px-Angelica_Kauffmann_002.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Monk of Calais (1780) by Angelica Kauffman, depicting Pastor Yorick exchanging snuffboxes with Father Lorenzo \"...